==Bulgarian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|bg|sla-pro|*večerъ}}, from {{inh|bg|ine-pro|*wekʷsperos}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{bg-IPA|ве́чер}}

===Noun===
{{bg-noun|ве́чер|f|g2=m|adj=вече́рен}}

# [[evening]], [[eve]], [[eventide]]

====Usage notes====
* Declension as a masculine noun is archaic.

====Declension====
{{bg-ndecl|ве́чер<(f)>|title=Declension of ве́чер (normal feminine declension)}}
{{bg-ndecl|ве́чер<>|title=Declension of ве́чер (archaic masculine declension)}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|bg|вчера||yesterday}}
* {{l|bg|довечера||tonight, this evening}}
* {{l|bg|привечер||dusk}}
* {{l|bg|вечеря||dinner}}
** {{l|bg|вечерям||to dine}}
* {{l|bg|вечерня||evening event}}
* {{l|bg|навечерие||almost eve}}
* {{l|bg|вечерница||Evening star (Venus)}}
* {{l|bg|свечерявам||to become evening, to dusk}}

===Adverb===
{{head|bg|adverb|head=ве́чер}}

# in the [[evening]]

